{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02392",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.29,
      "end_seconds": 5.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Okay, afternoon, thanks for coming in. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.3,
      "end_seconds": 13.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Well, uh, I've been having burning pain in the upper tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.98,
      "end_seconds": 17.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.09,
      "end_seconds": 23.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, it's been about a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.92,
      "end_seconds": 26.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. What aggravates it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.01,
      "end_seconds": 31.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "I notice it more with an empty stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.55,
      "end_seconds": 35.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "So, does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.79,
      "end_seconds": 43.01,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Indigestion goes along with it, um, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.45,
      "end_seconds": 47.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Okay, have you had pain at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.24,
      "end_seconds": 67.58,
      "duration_seconds": 15.34,
      "text": "Mm, yes, about the same, two weeks. With pain at night, honestly, on and off. Yeah, the indigestion? That's been for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.72,
      "end_seconds": 72.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Any difficulty swallowing or weight loss at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.85,
      "end_seconds": 78.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "No, um, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.11,
      "end_seconds": 83.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.62,
      "text": "Alright, have you noticed vomiting blood or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.45,
      "end_seconds": 88.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Oh, no, no vomiting blood or black stools."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.15,
      "end_seconds": 92.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.58,
      "end_seconds": 97.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.33,
      "end_seconds": 103.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.26,
      "end_seconds": 124.8,
      "duration_seconds": 20.54,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions. No, I've never smoked in my life. My husband and I live above the shop. I retired from the post office two years ago. I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.67,
      "end_seconds": 142.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.97,
      "end_seconds": 152.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "Uh, I've had arthritis in my knees for five years now. Um, I've had diabetes, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.46,
      "end_seconds": 165.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "Right, so diabetes is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.49,
      "end_seconds": 172.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Um, no, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.7,
      "end_seconds": 178.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.08,
      "end_seconds": 185.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "Erm, you know, I take diclofenac, 50 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.29,
      "end_seconds": 189.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.73,
      "end_seconds": 199.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.98,
      "end_seconds": 223.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 114 over 77, temperature is 36.9 degrees. And heart rate 81, oxygen saturation is 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.95,
      "end_seconds": 228.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.47,
      "end_seconds": 232.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.82,
      "end_seconds": 256.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Your upper tummy is tender in the middle with no guarding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.9,
      "end_seconds": 261.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Okay, please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.68,
      "end_seconds": 287.79,
      "duration_seconds": 16.11,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, this is probably a possible stomach ulcer from anti-inflammatory tablets. I'm going to order a blood count, for dyspepsia. I'll start you on omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day, eight weeks. It's for stomach ulcer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.29,
      "end_seconds": 291.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "That's simple enough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.16,
      "end_seconds": 303.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.7,
      "text": "Stop the ibuprofen and use paracetamol for the knee pain instead. I'll want another look in six weeks. So, does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.03,
      "end_seconds": 309.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Oh, no, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.81,
      "end_seconds": 312.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}